usage: generate.py [-h] [--model MODEL] [--duration DURATION]
                   [--num_samples NUM_SAMPLES]
                   [--diffusion_steps DIFFUSION_STEPS]
                   [--constraints CONSTRAINTS] [--output OUTPUT]
                   [--history_frames HISTORY_FRAMES] [--no-postprocess]
                   [--seed SEED] [--cfg_weight CFG_WEIGHT [CFG_WEIGHT ...]]
                   [--checkpoints_dir CHECKPOINTS_DIR]
                   prompt

Cmd line API for generating motions with Ardy

positional arguments:
  prompt                Text prompt describing the motion to generate.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model MODEL         Model nickname (core/g1/soma, optionally with horizon
                        like core8) or full folder name.
  --duration DURATION   Duration in seconds (default: 5.0)
  --num_samples NUM_SAMPLES
                        Number of samples to generate (default: 1)
  --diffusion_steps DIFFUSION_STEPS
                        Number of diffusion steps, at most the model's
                        schedule length (num_base_steps, the default).
  --constraints CONSTRAINTS
                        Saved constraint list
  --output OUTPUT       Output stem name: with one sample writes a single file
                        per format (e.g. test.npz, test.csv); with multiple
                        samples creates a folder and writes test_00.npz,
                        test_01.npz, ... inside it. Used for NPZ and CSV. Bare
                        names are written under outputs/; pass a path (e.g.
                        ./test or results/test) to write elsewhere.
  --history_frames HISTORY_FRAMES
                        History frames visible to each autoregressive step
                        (multiple of the model's token size). Default: the
                        longest history that fits the model's trained 10s
                        window; smaller values adapt faster but transition
                        more abruptly.
  --no-postprocess      Don't apply motion post-processing to reduce foot
                        skating (ignored for G1)
  --seed SEED           Seed for reproducible results
  --cfg_weight CFG_WEIGHT [CFG_WEIGHT ...]
                        CFG scale(s): one float (text weight only) or two
                        floats [text_weight, constraint_weight] (default: 2.0
                        2.0).
  --checkpoints_dir CHECKPOINTS_DIR
                        Local dir holding released model folders. Falls back
                        to the CHECKPOINTS_DIR env var; if neither is set the
                        model is downloaded from Hugging Face.
